IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art75a: Article 75a, supervisory and enforcement powers of the AI Office (inserted by the Omnibus, `▼M1 INSERTED`). LAYER 1.
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026). Only the amended text exists: the Article is new, and the amended text is in force from 27 July 2026, so no version split is needed.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 75a act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 75a(2) adopt a decision to start an investigation into the non-compliance`
    `Art 75a(2) notify the operator of the AI system concerned of the investigation`
    `Art 75a(2) send a request to the AI Office to assess the matter`
    `Art 75a(3) state the legal basis and the purpose of the request, specify the information required and set the period`
    `Art 75a(4) inform the provider concerned of the subject matter and purpose of the investigation, the relevant fines and the right to have the decision reviewed`
    `Art 75a(4) inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State before conducting the inspection`
    `Art 75a(4) afford the AI Office the necessary assistance to conduct its on-site inspection`
    `Art 75a(4) apply for the authorisation of a judicial authority`
    `Art 75a(4) verify promptly that the coercive measures envisaged are neither arbitrary nor excessive`
    `Art 75a(4) review the necessity of the investigation or inspection or demand information from the case file of the AI Office`
    `Art 75a(5) carry out an investigation, inspection or other fact-finding measure on behalf and for the account of the AI Office`
    `Art 75a(6) order operators to provide access to, and explanations relating to, their AI systems`
    `Art 75a(6) impose an obligation on an operator to retain all data and documents deemed to be necessary`
    `Art 75a(7) appoint independent external experts and auditors`
    `Art 75a(7) share the information obtained as a result of the monitoring actions with the relevant competent authorities of the Member States`
    `Art 75a(8) use the information collected pursuant to this Article for a purpose other than the purpose of this Regulation`

DECLARE `Art 75a(4) power of the officials of the AI Office` IS ONE OF
    `Art 75a(4)(a) enter any of the business premises, land or property located in the Union of the operator concerned`
    `Art 75a(4)(b) examine the books, data and other material relevant to the execution of their tasks`
    `Art 75a(4)(c) take or obtain in any form copies of or extracts from books, data and other records`
    `Art 75a(4)(d) ask any of the persons subject to the inspection for oral or written explanations and record the answers`
    `Art 75a(4)(e) seal any business premises and books or records for the duration of, and to the extent necessary for, the inspection`
    `Art 75a(4) any other power that the list does not name`

§ `Article 75a(1): powers of a market surveillance authority, and cost recovery`

-- src:1199 | 1. When exercising its tasks of supervision and enforcement laid down in Article 75(1) of this Regulation, the AI Office shall have all the powers of a market surveillance authority provided for in this Section and in Article 14(4) and Article 16(3) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. The AI Office shall be authorised to fully reclaim from the relevant operator the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities with respect to instances of non-compliance, including costs for human and technical resources, in accordance with Article 15 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Article 17 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis.
@ref Art 75a(1) first sentence (src:1199)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office is exercising its tasks of supervision and enforcement laid down in Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(1) first sentence the AI Office has all the powers of a market surveillance authority provided for in this Section and in Article 14(4) and Article 16(3) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI Office is exercising its tasks of supervision and enforcement laid down in Article 75(1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When exercising its tasks of supervision and enforcement laid down in Article 75(1) of this Regulation, the AI Office shall have all the powers" (a grant gated by "when": split site (ii), fork F-75a-1-when)

-- src:1199 | 1. When exercising its tasks of supervision and enforcement laid down in Article 75(1) of this Regulation, the AI Office shall have all the powers of a market surveillance authority provided for in this Section and in Article 14(4) and Article 16(3) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. The AI Office shall be authorised to fully reclaim from the relevant operator the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities with respect to instances of non-compliance, including costs for human and technical resources, in accordance with Article 15 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Article 17 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis.
@ref Art 75a(1) second sentence (src:1199)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the costs are costs of the supervision and enforcement activities of the AI Office with respect to instances of non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are reclaimed from the relevant operator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(1) second sentence the AI Office is authorised to fully reclaim from the relevant operator the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the costs are costs of the supervision and enforcement activities of the AI Office with respect to instances of non-compliance` AND `the costs are reclaimed from the relevant operator`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the authorisation is limited to costs "with respect to instances of non-compliance" reclaimed "from the relevant operator", with no "only" (ruling (c))

-- src:1199 | 1. When exercising its tasks of supervision and enforcement laid down in Article 75(1) of this Regulation, the AI Office shall have all the powers of a market surveillance authority provided for in this Section and in Article 14(4) and Article 16(3) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. The AI Office shall be authorised to fully reclaim from the relevant operator the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities with respect to instances of non-compliance, including costs for human and technical resources, in accordance with Article 15 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Article 17 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis.
@ref Art 75a(1) third sentence (src:1199)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(1) third sentence Article 17 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 applies mutatis mutandis` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "Article 17 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis"

§ `Article 75a(2): investigations`

-- src:1200 | 2. Where the AI Office has reasonable grounds to suspect non-compliance with this Regulation by a provider or a deployer of an AI system referred to in Article 75(1) of this Regulation, it may adopt a decision to start an investigation into that non-compliance in accordance with Article 14(4), point (f) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Upon starting such an investigation, the AI Office shall notify the operator of the AI system concerned. The AI Office may exercise the powers referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article on its own initiative or following a complaint received pursuant to Article 85 of this Regulation, even before starting an investigation pursuant to Article 14(4), point (f) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.
@ref Art 75a(2) first sentence (src:1200)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has reasonable grounds to suspect non-compliance with this Regulation by a provider or a deployer of an AI system referred to in Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(2) first sentence the AI Office may adopt a decision to start an investigation into the non-compliance` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI Office has reasonable grounds to suspect non-compliance with this Regulation by a provider or a deployer of an AI system referred to in Article 75(1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the AI Office has reasonable grounds to suspect non-compliance ..., it may adopt a decision to start an investigation" (a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-75a-2-where)

-- src:1200 | 2. Where the AI Office has reasonable grounds to suspect non-compliance with this Regulation by a provider or a deployer of an AI system referred to in Article 75(1) of this Regulation, it may adopt a decision to start an investigation into that non-compliance in accordance with Article 14(4), point (f) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Upon starting such an investigation, the AI Office shall notify the operator of the AI system concerned. The AI Office may exercise the powers referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article on its own initiative or following a complaint received pursuant to Article 85 of this Regulation, even before starting an investigation pursuant to Article 14(4), point (f) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.
@ref Art 75a(2) first sentence (src:1200)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has reasonable grounds to suspect non-compliance with this Regulation by a provider or a deployer of an AI system referred to in Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75a act`
`Art 75a(2) first sentence the AI Office's choice to adopt a decision to start an investigation` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the AI Office has reasonable grounds to suspect non-compliance with this Regulation by a provider or a deployer of an AI system referred to in Article 75(1)`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MAY `Art 75a(2) adopt a decision to start an investigation into the non-compliance`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1200 | 2. Where the AI Office has reasonable grounds to suspect non-compliance with this Regulation by a provider or a deployer of an AI system referred to in Article 75(1) of this Regulation, it may adopt a decision to start an investigation into that non-compliance in accordance with Article 14(4), point (f) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Upon starting such an investigation, the AI Office shall notify the operator of the AI system concerned. The AI Office may exercise the powers referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article on its own initiative or following a complaint received pursuant to Article 85 of this Regulation, even before starting an investigation pursuant to Article 14(4), point (f) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.
@ref Art 75a(2) second sentence (src:1200)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has started an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(2) second sentence the AI Office must notify the operator of the AI system concerned` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI Office has started an investigation`
