§ `Article 75a(3): requests for information`

-- src:1202 | 3. The AI Office may exercise the powers listed in Article 14(4), points (a), (b) and (c) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(12) and (13) of this Regulation by simple request or by decision.
@ref Art 75a(3) first subparagraph (src:1202)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(3) first subparagraph the AI Office may exercise the powers listed in Article 14(4), points (a), (b) and (c) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(12) and (13) by simple request or by decision` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "The AI Office may exercise the powers ... by simple request or by decision"

-- Second subparagraph: the content of a request. A simple request and a request by decision each carry the common four indications, and then their own.
-- src:1203 | When requesting information, the AI Office shall state the legal basis and the purpose of the request, specify what information is required, and set the period within which the information is to be provided. Where the request is a simple request, the AI Office shall additionally indicate that although there is no obligation to provide the information requested, in the case of a voluntary reply, the information must be correct and not misleading, and indicate the potential fines provided for in Article 99(5) for supplying incorrect or misleading information. Where the request is made by decision, the AI Office shall additionally indicate the fines provided for in Article 99(5) for supplying incorrect, incomplete or misleading information and indicate the right to have the decision reviewed by the Court of Justice of the European Union. The AI Office shall send a copy of the request to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the operator or its legal representative is situated.
@ref Art 75a(3) second subparagraph (src:1203)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the request is made by decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request states the legal basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request states the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request specifies what information is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets the period within which the information is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request indicates that there is no obligation to provide the information requested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request indicates that a voluntary reply must be correct and not misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request indicates the potential fines provided for in Article 99(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request indicates the right to have the decision reviewed by the Court of Justice of the European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI Office has sent a copy of the request to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the operator or its legal representative is situated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(3) second subparagraph the request for information has the content that the AI Office must give it` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the request is made by decision`
         THEN JUST (    `the request states the legal basis` AND `the request states the purpose` AND `the request specifies what information is required` AND `the request sets the period within which the information is to be provided`
                    AND `the request indicates the potential fines provided for in Article 99(5)` AND `the request indicates the right to have the decision reviewed by the Court of Justice of the European Union`
                    AND `the AI Office has sent a copy of the request to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the operator or its legal representative is situated`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the AI Office shall state ... specify ... and set"; "Where the request is made by decision, the AI Office shall additionally indicate the fines ... and ... the right to have the decision reviewed"; "shall send a copy" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
         ELSE JUST (    `the request states the legal basis` AND `the request states the purpose` AND `the request specifies what information is required` AND `the request sets the period within which the information is to be provided`
                    AND `the request indicates that there is no obligation to provide the information requested` AND `the request indicates that a voluntary reply must be correct and not misleading` AND `the request indicates the potential fines provided for in Article 99(5)`
                    AND `the AI Office has sent a copy of the request to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the operator or its legal representative is situated`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the request is a simple request, the AI Office shall additionally indicate that although there is no obligation ..., in the case of a voluntary reply, the information must be correct and not misleading, and indicate the potential fines"

-- src:1203 | When requesting information, the AI Office shall state the legal basis and the purpose of the request, specify what information is required, and set the period within which the information is to be provided. Where the request is a simple request, the AI Office shall additionally indicate that although there is no obligation to provide the information requested, in the case of a voluntary reply, the information must be correct and not misleading, and indicate the potential fines provided for in Article 99(5) for supplying incorrect or misleading information. Where the request is made by decision, the AI Office shall additionally indicate the fines provided for in Article 99(5) for supplying incorrect, incomplete or misleading information and indicate the right to have the decision reviewed by the Court of Justice of the European Union. The AI Office shall send a copy of the request to the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the operator or its legal representative is situated.
@ref Art 75a(3) second subparagraph (src:1203)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office requests information in the exercise of the powers referred to in this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75a act`
`Art 75a(3) second subparagraph the AI Office's duty to give the request for information its content` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the AI Office requests information in the exercise of the powers referred to in this paragraph`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MUST `Art 75a(3) state the legal basis and the purpose of the request, specify the information required and set the period`
        HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 75a(4): inspections`

-- src:1204 | 4. In order to carry out the tasks assigned to it under this Section, the AI Office may conduct all necessary remote or on-site inspections pursuant to the powers laid down in Article 14(4), points (d) and (e) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(5) of this Regulation. When conducting an inspection, the AI Office shall inform the provider concerned of the subject matter and purpose of the investigation, the relevant fines referred to in Article 99(5) of this Regulation, and the right to have the decision reviewed by the Court of Justice of the European Union. Prior to conducting an inspection, the AI Office shall inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the operator or its legal representative is situated.
@ref Art 75a(4) first sentence (src:1204)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the inspection is necessary to carry out the tasks assigned to the AI Office under this Section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(4) first sentence the AI Office may conduct all necessary remote or on-site inspections` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the inspection is necessary to carry out the tasks assigned to the AI Office under this Section`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "all necessary" inspections "to carry out the tasks assigned to it under this Section", with no "only"

