-- src:1204 | 4. In order to carry out the tasks assigned to it under this Section, the AI Office may conduct all necessary remote or on-site inspections pursuant to the powers laid down in Article 14(4), points (d) and (e) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(5) of this Regulation. When conducting an inspection, the AI Office shall inform the provider concerned of the subject matter and purpose of the investigation, the relevant fines referred to in Article 99(5) of this Regulation, and the right to have the decision reviewed by the Court of Justice of the European Union. Prior to conducting an inspection, the AI Office shall inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State in the territory of which the operator or its legal representative is situated.
@ref Art 75a(4) third sentence (src:1204)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office is about to conduct an inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75a act`
`Art 75a(4) third sentence the AI Office's duty to inform the market surveillance authority before the inspection` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the AI Office is about to conduct an inspection`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MUST `Art 75a(4) inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State before conducting the inspection`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1205 | During such an inspection, the officials of the AI Office shall be empowered to:
-- src:1206 | (a) enter any of the business premises, land or property located in the Union of the operator concerned;
-- src:1207 | (b) examine the books, data and other material relevant to the execution of their tasks, irrespective of the medium on which they are stored;
-- src:1208 | (c) take or obtain in any form copies of or extracts from books, data and other records;
-- src:1209 | (d) ask any of the persons subject to the inspection, or their representatives, or staff, for oral or written explanations on factors or documents relating to the subject matter and purpose of the inspection, and to record the answers;
-- src:1210 | (e) seal any business premises and books or records for the duration of, and to the extent necessary for, the inspection.
@ref Art 75a(4) points (a) to (e) (src:1205-1210)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `an inspection of the AI Office is under way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power` IS A `Art 75a(4) power of the officials of the AI Office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(4) the officials of the AI Office are empowered to exercise the power during the inspection` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `the power`
         WHEN `Art 75a(4) any other power that the list does not name` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the officials of the AI Office shall be empowered to:" is followed by a list that no "only" closes
         OTHERWISE
             IF `an inspection of the AI Office is under way`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "During such an inspection, the officials of the AI Office shall be empowered to" (an unmet "during" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (c))

-- src:1211 | Where the AI Office finds that a natural or legal person opposes or obstructs an inspection, the national competent authority of the Member State concerned shall afford it the necessary assistance, requesting, where appropriate, the assistance of the police or an equivalent enforcement authority, to enable it to conduct its on-site inspection.
@ref Art 75a(4) assistance (src:1211)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office finds that a natural or legal person opposes or obstructs an inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75a(4) the national competent authority must afford the AI Office the necessary assistance to conduct its on-site inspection` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI Office finds that a natural or legal person opposes or obstructs an inspection`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the AI Office finds that a natural or legal person opposes or obstructs an inspection, the national competent authority ... shall afford it the necessary assistance" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b)) (fork F-75a-4-duty)

-- src:1211 | Where the AI Office finds that a natural or legal person opposes or obstructs an inspection, the national competent authority of the Member State concerned shall afford it the necessary assistance, requesting, where appropriate, the assistance of the police or an equivalent enforcement authority, to enable it to conduct its on-site inspection.
